\0
The planet Gunawan was the site of the largest single battle in the conflict. The planet's supply lines were severed, and the Freedom Guard stronghold in the capitol of Indra was besieged by a massive Imperium contingent. Indra's last line of defense was a canyon pass just outside the city. 
\1
Gunawan cannot stand. Loss of the planet will cripple our war effort, but supply ships have been unable to penetrate the Imperium’s blockade, and the besieged capitol of Indra is about to fall. An escape vessel has been waiting in orbit to evacuate key personnel if necessary. The Imperium is preparing for a massive assault on the canyon pass just outside the city. The escape ship will be ready in an hour. Hold the position and protect all Headquarters long enough for Radec and the rest of the Synod to escape the planet. Retreat is not an option. Do not attempt to relocate any structures. Destroy all Imperium air facilities to prevent the escape vessel from being attacked as it leaves the planet.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Protect all HQs to assure the security of\n
\s\s\s\s the Synod commanders\n 
-->  Create an aerial assault force and eliminate\n
\s\s\s\s all Imperium Rearming Decks within the hour
\2
Well done. Your perseverance is convincing.\n 
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Outnumbered and cut off, Freedom Guard forces in Indra entrenched and fought resolutely for several weeks. Over eighty percent of their number was lost in the conflict, although the casualties they inflicted on invading Imperium forces were even greater. As the city collapsed under a tremendous wave of Imperium armor, Freedom Guard Commander Radec and several other members of the Synod fled the planet and moved to Elmaean, where they attempted to marshal their  remaining forces to make a stand against the advancing Imperium tide. 
\3
Defeat is unacceptable.